    {
        "content": "<p>Could you clarify whether this project is vibe-coded?</p>",
        "id": 605354232,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782040826
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm a proffessional software engineer, i don't vibe code. But of course i use AI to assist me if that's the question.</p>",
        "id": 605356812,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1782041914
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don’t know what this “of course” means, and I don’t know what “assist” means. I asked because we have a channel dedicated to AI authored projects. And I personally think it would be a lot more “professional” as you wrote, to disclose use of AI assistance in your README, but of course you are free to do whatever you want with your GitHub README.</p>",
        "id": 605367253,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782046058
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is not an AI authored project and this is not an accademic project.</p>",
        "id": 605368073,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1782046390
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Your definition of proffessional and disclosing use of AI assistance are completely unrelated.<br>\nAs an exemple, Leo de moura is using AI  to write his lean code now and i don't see anything disclosed about this on any Lean Readme.</p>",
        "id": 605368662,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1782046628
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Leo discloses AI use in every single commit message. But again my initial question had to do with this Zulip instance organization. Moderators here obviously have nothing to say about your personal projects hosted elsewhere. Let’s not derail this thread further.</p>",
        "id": 605369673,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782047005
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree, but just to conclude, Commit != Readme. So please don't try to impose rules on others that Lean don't impose itself.</p>",
        "id": 605370052,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1782047156
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>New version 0.4.0, upgraded to lean 4.32.0 and :</p>\n<ul>\n<li>small improvements in Cache Aside algorithms (Cache and CacheSWR)</li>\n</ul>",
